[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]UI and Subtitles - Configurable Font and Text Size[/color][/b][/size]

Make cinematic subtitles smaller without shrinking your dialogue choices. Adjust subtitle, dialogue and selected interface text independently, and choose between the vanilla [b]Afacad[/b] font and [b]Alegreya[/b].

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Text controls[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Cinematic subtitles:[/color][/b] Spoken lines, speaker names and movie subtitles. Default: 75%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Dialogue choices:[/color][/b] Response choices and their quantity labels. Default: 100%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Gameplay subtitles:[/color][/b] Bottom-screen, accessibility and overhead NPC lines. The game's distance scaling remains active. Default: 100%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Subtitle and dialogue font:[/color][/b] Vanilla Afacad or Alegreya. Default: Alegreya.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Other UI text:[/color][/b] Separate size and font controls for supported labels in menus, settings, inventory descriptions, stats, the glossary, court and the journal. Default: 100%, with Keep current as the font choice.
[/list]

Each size control ranges from [b]25% to 200%[/b], in 5% menu steps. Percentages use the label's original size, including any style supplied by another mod. 100% keeps that size.

The two font selectors are independent. Other UI can keep its existing font or use Afacad or Alegreya. Both font families are included; language-specific fallback faces continue to come from the game.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]

Open [b]Mod Settings > UI and Subtitles - Configurable Font and Text Size[/b], change the values and choose [b]Apply[/b]. UI defaults and existing labels update progressively at startup, save loading or Apply. Menus inherit those defaults when opened; large Apply updates may take a few seconds. Reset restores the defaults above; turning Enabled off restores font and size values still controlled by this mod.

Without the menu, launch the game once, close it and edit [b]Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/UIAndSubtitles/settings.ini[/b]. Restart afterward. The included settings.ini.example lists the available values.

[b]Logging[/b] is optional and off by default. Enable it to write UI preparation reasons, style and template counts, update timings and font-load timings to [b]Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log[/b]. Selected fonts load at startup or settings changes.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]UI coverage[/color][/b][/size]

Other UI controls cover main-menu and title-screen text, settings, inventory names and descriptions, item tooltips, stats, the glossary, court, crafting, character development and the journal. UI styles and widget defaults are prepared at game load or settings changes, so opening a menu does not trigger another scaling pass. Shared UI styles also affect other labels that use them. Rich-text bodies are supported; separately authored spans and inline icons can retain their own formatting. Graphical lettering is unchanged. Panels are not resized or rearranged. Very large text may exceed the space available in the game's layout.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install UI-and-Subtitles-Configurable-Font-and-Text-Size.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive's Dawnwalker folder into your The Blood of Dawnwalker installation directory, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Credits and source[/color][/b][/size]

Font choice inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/217]Alternative Font - Alegreya by WinterElfeas[/url]. Its Nexus archive is not redistributed here.

Alegreya and Afacad are by their respective project authors, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. License notices are included. Thanks to the UE4SS contributors, the ue4ss-common contributors, and mmarcussa for Mod Setting Menu and its integration helper.

